Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: report 11be from build_features

LuCI decides whether the wireless "mode" (htmode) dropdown offers the
802.11be entries by probing the hostapd binary: /usr/share/rpcd/ucode/luci
runs `/usr/sbin/hostapd -v<feature>` for every feature LuCI can gate on
and reports a feature only when the command exits 0. main.c forwards
`-v<arg>` to has_feature() in src/utils/build_features.h, which is a
compile-time table of #ifdef branches.

This QSDK hostapd fork does build EHT: hostapd-full.config sets
CONFIG_IEEE80211BE=y, the Makefile turns that into -DCONFIG_IEEE80211BE,
and the driver side is complete too (iwinfo/luci-rpc already advertise
the 'be' hwmode from ath12k). Only build_features.h lacks the "11be"
entry, so `hostapd -v11be` exits 1 on a binary that is perfectly capable
of EHT, and LuCI hides the 802.11be htmode options.

Add the branch next to the 11ac/11ax ones. Nothing else changes: no new
compile-time capability, the probe just now reports what the build
already contains.

---
--- a/qca/src/network/services/hostapd/src/utils/build_features.h
+++ b/qca/src/network/services/hostapd/src/utils/build_features.h
@@ -15,6 +15,10 @@
 	if (!strcmp(feat, "11ax"))
 		return 1;
 #endif
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	if (!strcmp(feat, "11be"))
+		return 1;
+#endif
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211R
 	if (!strcmp(feat, "11r"))
 		return 1;
